instruction:
This task bundles several unfinished labs and projects from a computer
architecture / systems sequence. Work in `/workspace` and treat the repository
as an existing codebase with missing core routines, not as a blank-slate
implementation exercise.

You need to finish the missing work across these areas:

`Lab/lab01/`
Linked-list cycle detection.

`Lab/lab02/`
Bit operations, the 16-bit Galois LFSR, and the dynamic vector
implementation. Use `make bit_ops lfsr` and `make vector-test` in
`Lab/lab02/` when checking those pieces.

`Lab/lab03/` and `Lab/lab04/`
The RISC-V assembly exercises, including recursive factorial, list mapping,
calling-convention cleanup, and the discrete lookup routine. The Venus jar is
available at `Lab/tools/venus.jar`.

`Lab/lab07/`
Cache-blocked transpose for matrices whose dimensions are not guaranteed to
align with the block size.

`Lab/lab09/`
SSE SIMD conditional-sum implementations, including the unrolled version.

`Lab/lab10/`
Manual OpenMP parallelization for vector addition and dot products, with both
manual-reduction and OpenMP-reduction variants.

`Project/proj1/`
P3 PPM image I/O, steganography via blue-channel LSB extraction, and the
color-channel version of Conway's Game of Life on a toroidal image grid.

`Project/proj4/`
The matrix library, including allocation, slicing with reference counting,
element access, fill, arithmetic, multiplication, and exponentiation.

The tests call the following entry points directly, so keep these exact
signatures:

```c
int ll_has_cycle(node *head);
unsigned get_bit(unsigned x, unsigned n);
void set_bit(unsigned *x, unsigned n, unsigned v);
void flip_bit(unsigned *x, unsigned n);
void lfsr_calculate(uint16_t *reg);
vector_t *vector_new();
int vector_get(vector_t *v, size_t loc);
void vector_delete(vector_t *v);
void vector_set(vector_t *v, size_t loc, int value);
void transpose_blocking(int n, int blocksize, int *dst, int *src);
long long int sum_simd(int vals[NUM_ELEMS]);
long long int sum_simd_unrolled(int vals[NUM_ELEMS]);
void v_add_optimized_adjacent(double *x, double *y, double *z);
void v_add_optimized_chunks(double *x, double *y, double *z);
double dotp_manual_optimized(double *x, double *y, int arr_size);
double dotp_reduction_optimized(double *x, double *y, int arr_size);
Image *readData(char *filename);
void writeData(Image *image);
void freeImage(Image *image);
Color *evaluateOnePixel(Image *image, int row, int col);
Image *steganography(Image *image);
Color *evaluateOneCell(Image *image, int row, int col, uint32_t rule);
Image *life(Image *image, uint32_t rule);
int allocate_matrix(matrix **mat, int rows, int cols);
int allocate_matrix_ref(matrix **mat, matrix *from, int row_offset, int col_offset, int rows, int cols);
void deallocate_matrix(matrix *mat);
double get(matrix *mat, int row, int col);
void set(matrix *mat, int row, int col, double val);
void fill_matrix(matrix *mat, double val);
int add_matrix(matrix *result, matrix *mat1, matrix *mat2);
int sub_matrix(matrix *result, matrix *mat1, matrix *mat2);
int mul_matrix(matrix *result, matrix *mat1, matrix *mat2);
int pow_matrix(matrix *result, matrix *mat, int pow);
int neg_matrix(matrix *result, matrix *mat);
int abs_matrix(matrix *result, matrix *mat);
```
